  "notable_quotes": [
    "For intrinsic proton conduction, structure optimization is most important because it controls hopping-site spacing and dynamics; monocoordinated phosphates should be within 0.5 nm.",
    "Proton transport follows a Grotthuss hopping mechanism with low activation energy, promoted by rotation of aligned phosphate ligands.",
    "The framework is thermally stable in its original crystal structure from 25 to 150 °C, but becomes amorphous at 180 °C."
